Day 3 — Azure Networking (VNet, NSG, Load Balancer, Application Gateway)

STAR-based DevOps Interview Questions

1️⃣ You need to design a secure multi-tier application in Azure. How will you structure VNets, subnets, and routing?

2️⃣ A VM in a private subnet cannot access the internet for updates. How will you troubleshoot and fix this in Azure?

3️⃣ Your application must be accessible globally with low latency. Which Azure load balancing services will you choose and why?

4️⃣ You want to restrict traffic between subnets except on specific ports. How will you design this using NSGs?

5️⃣ A public-facing web app is under attack. How will you protect it using Azure networking and security services?

6️⃣ You need private connectivity between on-premises and Azure with predictable latency. How will you design the hybrid network?

7️⃣ An internal service must be accessible across multiple VNets and subscriptions. How will you enable secure connectivity?

8️⃣ You want to expose a private application to selected external partners only. How will you design this architecture?

9️⃣ Traffic must be routed based on URL paths and headers. Which Azure service will you use and how will you configure it?

🔟 You need session persistence for a stateful application. How will you configure load balancer settings in Azure?

1️⃣1️⃣ Network traffic costs are unexpectedly high between Azure resources. What will you analyze and optimize?

1️⃣2️⃣ You need to inspect and control outbound traffic from workloads. Which Azure networking components will you use?

1️⃣3️⃣ A VM loses connectivity after an NSG change. How will you systematically troubleshoot the issue?

1️⃣4️⃣ You need DNS-based traffic routing for multi-region failover. How will you design this using Azure services?

1️⃣5️⃣ Your security team wants full visibility into network traffic and flows. How will you enable monitoring and logging?
